---
id: com.example.hello-worker
name: Hello Worker
version: 0.1.0
---

One Cloudflare Worker that answers every request with a greeting and the current time, deployed from a sandbox with
no Cloudflare account and handed to its reader to claim.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term       | URI                          |
| ---------- | ---------------------------- |
| `type`     | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`      |
| `feat`     | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`      |
| `scenario` | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`  |
| `decision` | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`  |

## Types

```mdl
type Greeting
  desc: The JSON body the Worker answers every request with.
  fields:
    message: string        # a fixed greeting
    time: string           # the current time, ISO 8601 in UTC
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Greeting endpoint
  desc: One fetch handler, with no router, dependencies or build step beyond wrangler's own.

  req F-1.1: Every request, whatever its method or path, is answered with `type:Greeting` as JSON.
  req F-1.2: `time` is the moment the request was served, in UTC.
```

F-2 to F-4 are named on the project's feature map — Deploy without an account, Verified response, Claimed
account — and are not written yet. Each gets a `feat` block here, with its requirements, before the implementation is
planned.

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: The Worker greets
  when: a client fetches any path on the Worker
  then: the response is `type:Greeting` with `time` within a minute of the request
```

## Changelog

Every change to this spec adds a decision, newest last. See `lang/changelog.mdl` for the attribution rules.

```mdl
decision D-1: The Hello Worker template seeds this spec partly written, with the project's features filed against it and a partial task list; the assistant completes the spec, plans the implementation as tasks and works them until the Worker answers.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:dmaretskyi
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The seeded spec states `type:Greeting` and [F-1] in full and only names F-2 to F-4, which the assistant writes from the feature map. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
  why: The endpoint is the part a reader can state up front; the deploy, its verification and the claim are where the agent's plan has to meet wrangler's real behaviour.
  rejected: Seeding every feat block with placeholder requirements, which the dialect would accept but which reads as a finished spec.
```

---

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

Extension block types used in this document are defined below using
the core `ext` primitive — the only construct the base language provides.

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap        # name[?]: TypeExpr  (# inline comment)
    literals?: UnionList     # a | b | c
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self              # feat blocks may contain feat blocks
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

`decision` is defined in [`changelog.mdl`](https://github.com/dxos/dxos/blob/main/packages/reflect/deus/lang/changelog.mdl).
